    "text": "Let the lines <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mfenced><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mfenced><mover><mi>z</mi><mo>&#175;</mo></mover></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mfenced><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mover><mi>z</mi><mo>&#175;</mo></mover><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo></math> (here <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></math>) be normal to a circle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi></math>. If the line <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>i</mi><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mover><mi>z</mi><mo>&#175;</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;is tangent to this circle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi></math>, then its radius is :",
